WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.830
For 20 years the field insisted sugar broke down through a compound called

2
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:13.370
methylglyoxal, and the theory had an enforcer: Carl Neuberg defended it and also

3
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.250
edited the leading biochemical journal.

4
00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:19.543
In Frankfurt, Gustav Embden kept finding something else.

5
00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:24.503
Working under a standard he stated as "meticulous cleanliness and rigorous

6
00:00:24.503 --> 00:00:29.863
accuracy," he turned up a three-carbon molecule again and again, and the consensus

7
00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.703
kept waving it off as contamination.

8
00:00:32.603 --> 00:00:34.943
Embden trusted the molecule over the consensus.

9
00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:41.297
In 1932 he concluded that the phosphoglyceric acid was being converted to pyruvic

10
00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:47.137
acid, laid out a unified scheme of glycolysis, and to get around Neuberg's editorial

11
00:00:47.137 --> 00:00:52.257
grip published it in a clinical journal rather than the biochemical one Neuberg

12
00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:56.937
controlled. It was the first correct map of how a cell pulls energy from glucose

13
00:00:56.937 --> 00:00:57.937
without oxygen.

14
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.860
His heart failed in 1933 as the Nazis dismantled his institute and dismissed his

15
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:04.860
Jewish colleagues.

16
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.580
Across much of Europe the pathway still bears his name first: Emden Meyerhof Parnas.
